 "objective": "Audit the 22 `partial def` constants and their `._unsafe_rec` companions found by the L1 baseline (list in baseline/audit/axiom-audit.json summary.partial_declarations) and decide, per constant, whether it is proof-relevant: can any theorem's statement or proof term depend on the partial constant in a way that inhabits an uninhabited type? Confirm the kernel/compiler boundary for `partial` (safety=partial, not unsafe) and extend the L1 forbidden scanner with a distinct `partial` classification so future baselines report it explicitly rather than folding it into defs.",
 "deps": [
  "longrun/results/L1-lean-baseline.json (summary.partial_declarations, 22 names)",
  "baseline/audit/declarations.tsv (per-declaration kind + cone)",
  "baseline/audit/dep-edges.tsv (reverse use of each partial constant)",
  "release/ @ the 462-file hash manifest recorded in the L1 card"
 ],
 "lane": "verifier",
 "acceptance": "Constructed input: a Lean probe that (a) re-lists every safety=partial constant in the 454 built modules, (b) computes the transitive dependent set of each from the compiled environment, (c) for every dependent theorem prints its type and flags any whose type is a `False`/empty-type-shaped proposition or whose proof term uses the partial constant in a non-eliminated position. Downstream consumer: the L1 result card's partial-declaration section and the extended scanner are re-run over release/. Independent rebuild: fresh `lake build` exit 0 and the probe recompiled in a clean worktree. Semantic review: a result card under longrun/results/ classifies each of the 22 constants (proof-irrelevant / eliminated-by-kernel / needs repair), states whether the D6/D13 treatment (informational) is correct, and ends TASK_DONE/TASK_BLOCKED. No release source may be modified.",
 "host_pool": [
  "ophis-gpu"
 ],
 "requires_lean": true,
 "max_hours": 6,
 "expected_evidence": "partial-def-audit.json with per-constant dependent sets and type shapes; scanner update; card with verdict",
 "created_by": "L1-lean-baseline",
 "created_at": "2026-09-11T15:52:00Z",
 "notes": "Not a duplicate: L1-C1 replays the axiom audit; this task is the semantic partial-definition boundary review that the L1 baseline explicitly left as informational."
